 - **Details.** A skill opens the floating Details with its size, its source, a state switch (On, Name only, Off; Codex has On and Off; a plugin skill and Cursor have none) and the skill's note, one sentence on what its state means for the list (some skills have none). A press adds one `skill.rule` row to the tray; while the row waits, the pressed state shows a solid ring in the preview colour on the preview fill (`.ctx-switch button.pending`). The rule is the Library's, so Apply, backup, verify and Undo are unchanged.
 - **How this is counted.** A folded list under the picture: where the last list came from, the rule and the date it was checked, and what is not measured. It stays open across a redraw. Paths and log names live only here and in Details.
 - **Toast.** After Apply: "Applied 2 changes. The backup is in Changes. Your next chat will show the real list." with Undo ("Undo all" for two or more changes).
